Fixed all four review findings in `src/lsp.rs`:

- Range `to` after an `lru_cache` variable is no longer mistaken for a decorated declaration; decorators must be first on their line and share the `to` line.
- Keyword-started parameterless literals (`to give back 42 end`) now push a `Literal` frame, so their `end` no longer closes the enclosing scope.
- The 5000-line benchmark now asserts a 2-second bound; the report is synced.
- EOF now closes `closes_at_newline` literal frames, and line-end completion does too.

Added three regression tests and updated `phases/phase-075/REPORT.md`. All four gates pass: `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `cargo test --all-targets` (2776 passed), and `../rbops/verify.sh "phase-075"`.
